    "id": "nr-llr-derate-matching-baselines",
    "issue": "eda07788",
    "purpose": "consumer-family",
    "description": "Exploratory pilot for 5G NR LDPC LLR de-rate-matching: target_n channel LLRs mapped onto the full_n mother-code positions, with the 2Z punctured prefix and untransmitted parity at zero and fillers at a known-zero LLR. gf2 Nr5gRateMatchedCode::prepare_llrs is the baseline arm; AFF3CT v4.7.0 Puncturer_5G::depuncture behind a whole-consumer adapter (float conversion, zeroed output, filler normalization, conversion back to Vec<Llr>) is the candidate. Every configuration passed the committed equivalence gate. The baseline arm is always gf2 and the candidate is the arm whose lead needs attribution, so a speedup above 1 in a `-gap-` cell means AFF3CT is ahead and above 1 in the `-control-` cell means the native gf2 build is ahead of the conservative-portable control. The `-null-` identity cell measures the noise floor. Cells cover both base graphs, filler and filler-free codes and lifting sizes 22 to 96. This pilot sizes the family's measurement resolution; no cell decides adoption."
  },
  "frozen": {
    "frozen_utc": "2026-09-10T17:00:23Z"
  },
  "effect": {
    "worthwhile_speedup": null,
    "rationale": "Comparator-gap cells only. This issue is a baseline survey: it proposes no production change, so no worthwhile-speedup threshold applies and none is declared.",
    "measurement_resolution": null,
    "resolution_evidence": null,
    "equivalence_margin": 1.1,
    "equivalence_rationale": "A 10% equivalence margin, carried unchanged into the confirmatory addendum so the pilot's own decisions are computed under the rule the confirmation uses. Pilot cells never yield a pass; the margin exists here only to make the pilot's recorded decisions comparable.",
    "material_gap_threshold": 1.2,
    "material_gap_rationale": "A 20% whole-consumer wall-clock gap is the smallest gap between two arms of this operation worth attributing to a named cause (representation conversion, output initialization, per-call dispatch or scatter code generation) rather than host noise. The pilot checks that this threshold sits above the measured resolution before the confirmatory addendum freezes it."
  },
